  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "single foreground seed pixel",
  "path": "unbounded square spiral starting upward from the seed; directions repeat up, right, down, left with leg lengths 2, 2, 4, 4, 6, 6, and so on, clipping out-of-bounds steps and stopping before the first blocker pixel",
  "trajectory": "paint every in-bounds background pixel along the spiral with the seed color",
  "transform": "preserve the original seed and blocker pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 11x11 [observed]
  background: 0 (black)
  seed:
    color: 3 (green), exactly 1 pixel
    position: near grid center, min distance to any edge >= 4 [observed]
  blockers:
    color: 2 (red), count 0-10 pixels
    placement: scattered; at least 1 must lie on the spiral path to terminate it (unless count=0)
    constraint: no blocker adjacent to seed (min Manhattan distance >= 2)
  spiral:
    direction_order: up, right, down, left (repeating)
    leg_lengths: 2, 2, 4, 4, 6, 6, 8, 8, ... (each length used twice, +2 after pair)
    clipping: out-of-bounds steps skipped but counted toward leg length
    termination: stop before the first blocker encountered on the in-bounds path; if no blocker, spiral fills until max_leg_length exceeded
    painted_pixels: 5-59 (varies by blocker proximity and grid bounds)
  output:
    same shape as input; all bg cells on spiral before first blocker painted with seed color; seed and blockers preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Create 11x11 grid of zeros.
    2. Place seed (color 3) near center (row 3-7, col 3-7, ensuring min edge distance >= 4).
    3. Compute the full spiral path from seed (all in-bounds positions).
    4. Choose a desired spiral length (painted pixels 5-60); pick a path index for the terminating blocker. Place that blocker (color 2) at the corresponding spiral position.
    5. Scatter 0-9 additional blocker pixels on cells NOT on the spiral path before the terminating blocker (they may be on the path after the terminator, or off-path entirely). Ensure min Manhattan distance >= 2 from seed.
    6. The input is the grid with only seed + blockers on bg. Output is derived by running the spiral painter.
```
